                <pb facs="0193" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89France/321: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-06-15T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 15, 1926—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>174. Referring to your telegram 224 of June 4, 11 a.m., information of the
                    Department is that the order placing an embargo against Boue Soeurs was revoked
                    June 8.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
